# Goose Repository Analysis: Agentic Harness Architecture

Comprehensive deep-dive into Block's Goose (AAIF fork), one of 8 agent orchestration frameworks. All findings cite concrete file paths and line numbers.

---

## 1. Project Identity & Purpose

**What is Goose?** 
Goose is an open-source, general-purpose AI agent that runs natively on macOS, Linux, and Windows. It's a complete desktop/CLI/API agent framework designed for code, workflows, research, writing, automation, and data analysis.

**Problem Domain:**
- Local-first AI agent execution (not cloud-locked)
- Framework for composable agent workflows (recipes)
- Extension ecosystem via Model Context Protocol
- Multiple LLM provider support with unified interface
- Human-in-the-loop decision making with permission model

**Source:** [README.md](reference/goose/README.md#L1-L30) — "your native open source AI agent — desktop app, CLI, and API"

