## 5. Agent Architecture

### 5a. Main Agent Loop / Control Flow

**Primary Entry Point:** [state_machine/session.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/agents/state_machine/session.rs#L1-L70)

The agent uses a **state machine pattern** replacing a legacy agent loop. Enabled via `GOOSE_STATE_MACHINE=1` environment variable.

**State Machine Core** ([goose-agent/machine.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose-agent/src/machine.rs#L48-L180)):

```rust
pub struct StateMachine<'a, S, E = ConversationEffect> {
    steps: Vec<Step<'a, S, E>>,
    cancel: CancellationToken,
}

impl<'a, S, E> StateMachine<'a, S, E> {
    pub async fn step(&self, session: &S, emit: &Emitter) -> Result<Option<StepResult<E>>>
    pub async fn apply<R>(...) -> Result<()>
    pub async fn run<R>(...) -> Result<S>
}
```

**Step Execution Model:**
1. **Step** = `Operation | Inference`
2. Each step runs sequentially
3. Returns `OperationResult::NotApplicable` or `OperationResult::Applied(StepResult)`
4. Results applied via `EffectHandler::apply_effects()`
5. Loop continues until `yield_to_client = true` or no applicable steps

**Conceptual Flow:**
```
User Message (persisted to session)
        ↓
Load Session (conversation history)
        ↓
StateMachine::step()
  ├─ EntryHookOperation         (pre-processing hooks)
  ├─ RecipeOperation             (if recipe active, execute recipe step)
  ├─ SkillOperation              (execute /skill commands)
  ├─ SlashCommandOperation       (execute /commands)
  ├─ SteerOperation              (steering queue from system)
  ├─ ProjectOperation            (project-aware tools)
  ├─ RetryOperation              (auto-retry logic)
  ├─ InferenceRunner             (→ call LLM provider)
  ├─ ToolExecutionOperation      (execute tool calls from LLM)
  ├─ UnknownToolOperation        (handle unrecognized tools)
  ├─ ToolApprovalOperation       (ask human before tool execution)
  ├─ BangShellOperation          (! command in agent message)
  ├─ ToolPairCompactionOperation (combine consecutive tool calls)
  ├─ CompactionOperation         (context summarization)
  ├─ MaxTurnsOperation           (enforce turn limit)
  ├─ DoctorOperation             (diagnostic info)
  ├─ ExitOnErrorOperation        (halt on error)
  └─ StopHookOperation           (policy hooks, can block turn end)
        ↓
Apply Effects (message append, replace conversation, update meta)
        ↓
If yield_to_client: return to UI/CLI
Else: loop back to StateMachine::step()
```

**Source:** [state_machine/mod.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/agents/state_machine/mod.rs#L1-L40)

### 5b. Architecture Style
- **Single-agent**: One active agent per session, but can spawn sub-agents via task tool
- **Hierarchical planner-executor**: Not explicit; recipes provide planning
- **ReAct-inspired**: Tool calls → results → next reasoning loop
- **Streaming first**: All provider calls support streaming

