**Message Model** ([conversation/message.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/conversation)):
- `Message` with role (user/assistant/system), content blocks
- Content blocks: Text, ToolRequest (call), ToolResult, Thinking, NotificationBlock
- Metadata: visibility, inference metadata, token usage

### 5d. Message/History Representation

**Conversation Object** ([conversation/mod.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/conversation)):
```rust
pub struct Conversation {
    messages: Vec<Message>,
    summary: Option<String>,  // If compacted
    // Context window management
}
```

**Message Content Blocks:**
- `Text(String)` — plain text
- `ToolRequest(ToolRequest)` — LLM → tool call
- `ToolResult(ToolResult)` — tool output back to LLM
- `Thinking(String)` / `RedactedThinking(String)` — model reasoning (Claude only)
- `SystemNotification(...)` — agent/system messages to user

**Compaction Strategy** ([context_mgmt/compact_messages.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/context_mgmt)):
- Triggered when context > DEFAULT_COMPACTION_THRESHOLD (8K tokens)
- LLM summarizes conversation into `summary` field
- Original messages can be dropped or marked hidden
- Compaction is re-entrant; can happen mid-session

