## 7. Tool System

### 7a. MCP-First Architecture

Goose is **MCP-centric**: All external tools are Model Context Protocol servers.

**MCP Protocol Version:** `ProtocolVersion::V_2025_11_25` ([agent.rs line 98](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/agents/agent.rs#L98))

**MCP Client Implementation** ([mcp_client.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/agents/mcp_client.rs#L1-L100)):
- Uses `rmcp` crate (Rust MCP reference implementation v3.0.0)
- Implements `McpClientTrait` with methods:
  - `list_tools()` — fetch tool schemas
  - `call_tool()` — execute tool with arguments
  - `read_resource()` — access MCP resources (prompts, docs)
  - `get_prompt()` — dynamic prompt extraction
- Supports streaming tool results
- Connection pooling & client reuse per extension

### 7b. Built-In MCP Servers

From [builtin_extension.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose/src/builtin_extension.rs) and [goose-mcp/mcp_server_runner.rs](reference/goose/crates/goose-mcp/src/mcp_server_runner.rs):

```rust
pub static BUILTIN_EXTENSIONS: Lazy<HashMap<&'static str, SpawnServerFn>> = Lazy::new(|| {
    HashMap::from([
        builtin!(autovisualiser, AutoVisualiserRouter),
        builtin!(computercontroller, ComputerControllerServer),
