## 18. Notable Idioms / Patterns

### 1. State Machine Architecture
- **Ordered operations** running sequentially
- **Re-entrant loops**: Multiple turns within single `StateMachine::step()`
- **Effect-based mutations**: Changes returned as `GooseEffect` enum
- **Persistence layer**: Effects applied via `SessionManager` (EffectHandler trait)

**Why This Pattern?**
- Testability: Operations are composable, testable in isolation
- Debuggability: Clear step-by-step execution trace
- Extensibility: New operations added as new Step types

### 2. MCP-First Extensions
- **Zero built-in tools** (except shell/file via developer extension)
- **All tools pluggable**: Even core tools (memory, vision) are MCP servers
- **Uniform interface**: Tool discovery via MCP ListTools
- **Extensible SDK**: Easy to create custom MCP servers in any language

### 3. Recipe-Driven Workflows
- **Declarative planning**: YAML templates for multi-turn flows
- **Composable sub-recipes**: Recipes can include other recipes
- **Parameterized inputs**: Template variables for reusability
- **Structured outputs**: JSON schema validation of results

### 4. Permission Model
- **Three-layer approval**: Rules, LLM judge, user confirmation
- **Granular tool categorization**: Shell vs Read vs Write
- **Policy hooks**: Can block turn-end if conditions unmet
- **Audit trail**: All approvals logged with metadata

### 5. Prompt Engineering
- **Embedded templates**: Jinja2 markdown files, compiled into binary
- **User customization**: Override any prompt at `~/.config/goose/prompts/`
- **Dynamic context injection**: Extensions, hints, mode flags injected at runtime
- **Multimodal support**: Separate prompts for vision, code modes

### 6. Session Persistence
- **SQLite per-session**: Lightweight, embedded DB
- **Lazy loading**: Conversation only loaded when needed
- **Incremental append**: Messages added one-by-one (no full rewrite)
- **Compaction support**: Conversation can be summarized in-place

### 7. Provider Abstraction
- **Trait-based polymorphism**: `Provider` trait covers all LLM backends
- **Declarative config**: Many providers built from YAML templates
- **Custom auth flows**: OAuth, API keys, client certs all supported
- **Streaming-first API**: All responses streamed, batched results supported

### 8. Context Management
- **Automatic compaction**: Context window triggers summarization
- **Token counting**: Multiple strategies (exact, estimated)
- **Message visibility**: Can hide/show messages from UI or LLM
- **Dual-visibility**: user_visible vs agent_visible (privacy)

